In 1991 Green project(James Gosling)
It was named as "Oak" in 1991
In 1992 Start7 demo a handheld prototype 
In 1995 it was renamed as Java(May)
In 1996 JDK 1.0 is released
The idea of java is "Write once,Run Anywhere" which means compile once into portable bytecode,Any device with Java Virtual Machine(JVM) can run it-no rewrite needed.
Java 1.0(Jan 1996)-JVM ,core libraries,applets-"Write once,Run Anywhere"
Java 5(Sep 2004)-Generic,annotations,enums,enhanced for-loop
Java 8(May 2014)-Lambdas,Stream API,new date/time API(LTS-standard)
Java 11(Sep 2018)-First LTS of the 6-month era;standard HTTP client

